  "id": "coldwaterwaterworks",
  "note": "COLDWATER WATERWORKS: the plant at the head of Ironside Street that every tap in Coldwater\nruns from (docs/systems-water-supply.md).\n\nThe tile's prose: a long brick engine house with tall arched windows and a slate roof, two open\nbeds behind it along the shore. The beds are their own tiles (Waterworks Settling Beds).\n\nSo it is a red-brick hall a little under two storeys, on a stone plinth, with five tall arched\nwindows along the front under stone hoods and the door in the middle, under a stone pediment that\ncarries the name, once, painted (`bare`). The roof is slate, stepped to a ridge, with a louvred\nlantern along it for the pump heat. The old boiler chimney still stands at the back corner, from\nbefore the pumps went electric. A blue main comes out of the east flank and dives into the ground.\nThe flanks carry two more arched windows each; the back has a roller door for plant.\n\nThe palettes are brick (`ty_ff_brick`), stone trim and slate. The blue is `ty_mains_engine`,\nthe Halcyon Fields Pumping Station's pump blue, because it is the same pipe.",
  "pal": "ty_ff_brick",
